# load_balance_p4rtl.sdc -- constraint-file SKELETON for board 'Terasic DE2-115'
# Generated by p4-to-rtl's --board flag. STRUCTURAL SKELETON ONLY --
# never synthesized/implemented against real hardware in this project.
# device_part: EP4CE115F29C7 (verified)
#   Quartus Prime 25.1std has FITTED three designs for this part from this repository (hw/de2-115/step{1_bringup,2_enet,2_host}, Timing Models: Final), and the fit placed 106-126 pins at locations cross-checked against the Terasic user manual by common/make_pins.py -- a package pinout that would not all be legal for a different device. The part number is therefore no longer a guess. What is still NOT established is that any PARTICULAR physical board carries it: Terasic has shipped more than one DE2-115 revision, so check your own board's System Builder output before programming anything that drives a shared bus.
# Pin/ball locations are intentionally NOT filled in below -- copy them
# from your board's official reference constraint file before using this
# for a real bitstream.

